Europe at the end of 1918 a horrific war  has been raging for the last four years  in the aftermath of the fighting the  world order changed this is what  happened and why the history of the  First World War and it's aftermath  industrialization revolutionized the war  tanks aircraft and machine guns were  deployed for the first time  poison gas killed tens of thousands and  some days as many as 60 thousand  soldiers fell on the western southern  and eastern fronts the Armistice of  Campania signed on the 11th of November  1918 brought the fighting to an end  Germany and her allies surrendered after  1,500 days of war 11 million were killed  20 million wounded or maimed the first  world war was the first truly global  conflict plunging 40 countries into the  fighting four of the great powers were  overwhelmed revolution swept Russia and  Germany whose rulers were deposed  Germany became a democracy  austro-hungary and the Ottoman Empire  were broken up the people's which have  made up the dominions were left in limbo  the victors hope to establish a new  order at the Versailles Conference  France Britain and the u.s. made most of  the decisions behind closed doors new  borders were drawn up for Europe Africa  and the Middle East  [Music]  but the vanquished felt hard done by  especially the Germans they protested  against the huge reparations imposed on  Germany to compensate for the damage  inflicted by the war against the  reduction in size of the German army and  against the loss of German territory  amounting to 10% America's President  Woodrow Wilson had another plan for  keeping the peace he founded the League  of Nations the forerunner of today's  United Nations but he failed to secure  the backing he needed at home the u.s.  never joined the league the organization  was weakened from the beginning the  victorious powers hoped the Treaty of  Versailles would ensure peace but their  plan fails poverty and frustration among  the losers created the conditions for  another war within just a few years  popular anger in Germany helped to bring  Hitler to power the dictator was  obsessed with sweeping away the  humiliations of the Treaty of Versailles  by going to war again the first world  war was the greatest catastrophe of the  20th century sowing the seeds for the  next even more destructive war  [Music]
 

